# Restarting Cuttle Flask

## When a restart is actually needed
- **Python code changes** (`src/api/web_chat_api.py`, `pipeline_trigger_executor.py`, anything Flask imports): daemon runs Flask with `FLASK_ENV=production` (no Werkzeug reloader). Changes need a Flask restart.
- **Pipeline JSON** (`src/pipelines/*.json`): hot-reloaded (~2s). **No restart.**
- Frontend HTML/JS/CSS: usually hard-refresh only.

## Ask before you restart (required)
The user often uses Cuttle from a **LAN device** (phone / another PC) and **cannot reach the tray icon**. Do **not** treat “tell them to use the tray” as the default.

1. Finish the work and deliver the reply first when possible.
2. Tell them plainly that Python changes need a Flask restart, then **emit the `flask.restart` action form** (below) instead of asking them to type a command. Never ask “OK to restart Flask now?” as bare prose.
3. Only restart after they click / approve. Never surprise-kill Flask.
4. If they say no / defer: leave Flask alone and note that the new code is not live yet.

### Ask with a card, not a sentence (required in Cuttle chat)

`.cuttle_global/actions/flask-restart.yaml` (`flask.restart`) and `.cuttle_global/actions/flask-health.yaml`
(`flask.health`) are allowlisted, so the ask should always be clickable — the user is often on a
phone / LAN device where typing `/restart graceful` is the worst available option. Emit this and
let them click; do **not** run the restart yourself.

**Do not** write the raw opening tag name in prose/backticks in the same message (e.g. explaining
the markup). A bare `<` + `cuttle_action_form` + `>` used to be parsed as a form open and could
swallow the real card. Prefer “action form” / “restart card” in prose; only emit the real
tagged JSON block for the live card.

```text
<cuttle_action_form>
{"mode":"choice","title":"Restart Flask (daemon-owned)","lock":"form","silent":true,"options":[
  {"id":"status","label":"Status — show restart state + active work","action":"flask.restart","params":{"mode":"status"}},
  {"id":"graceful","label":"Graceful — restart now (rejects if busy)","action":"flask.restart","params":{"mode":"graceful"}},
  {"id":"when-idle","label":"When idle — wait for active jobs to finish","action":"flask.restart","params":{"mode":"when-idle"}},
  {"id":"force","label":"Force — interrupt active work","action":"flask.restart","params":{"mode":"force"}},
  {"id":"health","label":"Health check only (no restart)","action":"flask.health","params":{}}
]}
</cuttle_action_form>
```

The action script adds `confirm: true` for `force` and posts `chat_notify: false`, so the restart
writes **no ack/completion bubbles**. The card reports it instead: it collapses to a one-line status
with a spinner while waiting/restarting, then a green check (`Flask restarted — PID …, 6.8s`) or a
red mark on failure. The card also carries its own `session_id`, so a click always reports back to
the chat the card came from — never a different one. Keep `silent` true.

All Flask-restart controller cards share form id `flask-restart-g{generation}` across chats until
the daemon replaces Flask (generation bumps). Clicking one settles the others; agents must not
invent a custom form `id`.

The `/restart …` slash commands below are the **fallback** — use them when the surface has no action
buttons (Discord, plain API callers) or when the user asks for the command by name.

### Why this matters (dogfooding)
Restarting Flask mid-run by `taskkill` on `web_chat_api` **destroys the chat that is waiting for your reply**. Cursor CLI may finish, but Cuttle never persists/delivers the answer. Ask → approve → use the **daemon-owned** restart path **after** the answer is out when you can; if the user only wants a restart, use `/restart` so an ack is persisted first.

## Correct procedure (daemon-owned; never kill yourself)

**After approval** (fallback when no action buttons are available), use chat:

```text
/restart graceful          # only if idle
/restart when-idle        # wait for active Cursor/Codex/jobs to finish
/restart force --yes      # interrupt active work (requires --yes)
/restart status            # show state + active tasks
```

Or `POST https://127.0.0.1:8080/api/flask/restart` with `{"mode":"graceful"}` (self-signed cert).

**Cursor hard gate:** project hook `.cursor/hooks.json` (`beforeShellExecution`) blocks
`taskkill`/`Stop-Process` targeting Cuttle-managed PIDs/cmdlines when the agent
workspace is this repo. Codex/Hermes do not have that gate (advisory via `AGENTS.md`
+ prompt injection only).

**One-time daemon restart** (loads watcher; run from a standalone terminal, not Cuttle chat):

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File /path/to/Cuttle/.cuttle\scripts\restart-daemon.ps1
```

Working directory for manual Start-Process must be `/path/to/Cuttle` with
`src\scripts\cuttle_daemon.py` (not `WD=src` + `src\scripts\...`).

Safe self-check (no stop/start):  

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File /path/to/Cuttle/.cuttle\scripts\restart-daemon.ps1 -DryRun
```

