### Do NOT (agents)
```powershell
# FORBIDDEN from Cursor/Codex/agent shells while chatting through Cuttle:
taskkill /F /PID …   # on web_chat_api
```
That is what caused lost completion messages.

### The trap
Daemon tracks the `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` **launcher**; the **`Python311\python.exe` child** holds port 8080. Killing only the launcher orphans the child → restart loop (“Flask unresponsive — restarting...”). The daemon’s coordinated restart kills the tree.

### Verify (HTTPS + self-signed on 8080)
```powershell
curl.exe -k -s -o NUL -w "%{http_code}" https://127.0.0.1:8080/api/health
# expect 200
curl.exe -k -s https://127.0.0.1:8080/api/flask/restart/status
```

## Don'ts
- Don't restart Flask without asking.
- Don't ask for restart approval in prose when `flask.restart` is available — emit the action form.
- Don't `taskkill` Flask from an agent that Flask is hosting.
- Don't kill only the launcher; coordinated restart handles the tree.
- Don't run a second `cuttle_daemon.py`.
- Don't kill `llama-server.exe` or unrelated `*MCP*` / UnityMCP processes.
- Full daemon restart only if the daemon itself is wedged: `.venv\Scripts\python.exe src\scripts\cuttle_daemon.py`.
- Don't report “restart complete” until `/api/health` (or restart status `healthy`) succeeds.
